  "justification": "This order ranks all 169 starting-hand classes from strongest to weakest by one objective measure: the share of the pot each hand wins when it is all in before the flop against a single opponent holding any random two cards. Each number was computed with this project's own equity calculator, using the class's lowest-numbered combo and every unseen combo as the opponent's range, then rounded to one decimal place. Hands with equal rounded numbers keep the starting-hand grid order. The order is used only to rebuild an opponent's preflop range at a width that matches how often that player has been seen raising or calling: the range is the shortest run of hands from the top of this list that covers the width, and it always holds at least a pair of aces.",
